 ## Socket access
 
-Use the socket path cmux provided before any default: `SOCK="${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-/tmp/cmux.sock}"`. Socket access can be off, restricted to cmux-spawned processes, or open to all local processes. If a command cannot connect, inspect `cmux capabilities --json` and `cmux ping` before changing settings.
+For this standard macOS release installation, the CLI is `/opt/homebrew/bin/cmux` and the socket is `$HOME/.local/state/cmux/cmux.sock`; expand HOME and pass the absolute path with `--socket`. This identifies the installed app, not permission to choose an existing window. A user-specified different instance requires its explicit socket path; if the socket is missing or ambiguous, ask instead of auto-discovering another instance. Socket access may require password authentication; let the official CLI read its saved password. Check capabilities and ping with that same explicit socket before requesting an authorization change.
 
